                <pb facs="0256" n="1216" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1216"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No.
                    85.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mariscal to Mr.
                            Bragg.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-06-28"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 28,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: In reply to your excellency’s note
                    of the 20th instant, relative to the case of the American citizen, B. B.
                    Glasier, imprisioned at Piedras Negras, I have the honor to inform you that a
                    report thereon has been requested by me from the authorities having cognizance
                    thereof.</p>
                <p>I reiterate, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Igno. Mariscal.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
